1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,463
First of all, let me thank you all for coming to this public meeting,

2
00:00:05,463 --> 00:00:07,130
to discuss the future of our town.

3
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:11,625
Our first speaker is Shona Ferguson, from Barford town council.

4
00:00:11,625 --> 00:00:12,330
Shona.

5
00:00:12,330 --> 00:00:13,071
Thank you.

6
00:00:13,071 --> 00:00:18,257
First I'll briefly give you some background information, then I'll be asking you for

7
00:00:18,257 --> 00:00:20,850
your comments on developments in the town.

8
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:25,709
Well, as you don't need me to tell you, Barford has changed a great

9
00:00:25,709 --> 00:00:27,791
deal in the last 50 years.

10
00:00:27,791 --> 00:00:30,220
These are some of the main changes.

11
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:36,070
Fifty years ago, buses linked virtually every part of the town and the neighbouring towns

12
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:36,850
and villages.

13
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:38,912
Most people used them frequently,

14
00:00:38,912 --> 00:00:40,149
but not now,

15
00:00:40,149 --> 00:00:45,510
because the bus companies concentrate on just the routes that attract most passengers.

16
00:00:45,510 --> 00:00:49,280
So parts of the town are no longer served by buses.

17
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:55,974
Even replacing old uncomfortable buses with smart new ones has had little impact on

18
00:00:55,974 --> 00:00:56,930
passenger numbers.

19
00:00:56,930 --> 00:01:00,118
It's sometimes said that bus fares are too high,

20
00:01:00,118 --> 00:01:05,077
but in relation to average incomes, fares are not much higher than they were

21
00:01:05,077 --> 00:01:06,140
50 years ago.

22
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:10,680
Changes in the road network are affecting the town.

23
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:16,165
The centre was recently closed to traffic on a trial basis, making it much

24
00:01:16,165 --> 00:01:17,340
safer for pedestrians.

25
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:20,020
The impact of this is being measured.

26
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:26,228
The new cycle paths, separating bikes from cars in most main roads, are being

27
00:01:26,228 --> 00:01:31,550
used far more than was expected, reducing traffic and improving air quality.

28
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:36,736
And although the council's attempts to have a bypass constructed have failed, we haven't

29
00:01:36,736 --> 00:01:40,810
given up hope of persuading the government to change its mind.

30
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:45,010
Shopping in the town centre has changed over the years.

31
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:49,390
Many of us can remember when the town was crowded with people going shopping.

32
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:55,498
Numbers have been falling for several years, despite efforts to attract shoppers, for instance

33
00:01:55,498 --> 00:01:57,680
by opening new car parks.

34
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:02,560
Some people combine shopping with visits to the town's restaurants and cafes.

35
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:06,152
Most shops are small independent stores，which is good,

36
00:02:06,152 --> 00:02:12,936
but many people prefer to use supermarkets and department stores in nearby large towns, as there are

37
00:02:12,936 --> 00:02:15,330
so few well-known chain stores here.

38
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:21,530
Turning now to medical facilities, the town is served by family doctors in several

39
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:24,630
medical practices - fewer than 50 years ago,

40
00:02:24,630 --> 00:02:27,730
but each catering for far more patients.

41
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,447
Our hospital closed 15 years ago,

42
00:02:30,447 --> 00:02:34,070
which means journeys to other towns are unavoidable.

43
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:38,340
On the other hand, there are more dentists than there used to be.

44
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:42,820
Employment patterns have changed, along with almost everything else.

45
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:48,000
The number of schools and colleges has increased, making that the main employment sector.

46
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,688
Services, such as website design and accountancy, have grown in importance,

47
00:02:52,688 --> 00:02:58,655
and surprisingly, perhaps, manufacturing hasn't seen the decline that has affected it in other

48
00:02:58,655 --> 00:03:00,360
parts of the country.

49
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:08,814
Now I'll very quickly outline current plans for some of the town's facilities, before

50
00:03:08,814 --> 00:03:11,230
asking for your comments.

51
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:16,756
As you'll know if you regularly use the car park at the railway station,

52
00:03:16,756 --> 00:03:17,940
it's usually full.

53
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:22,918
The railway company applied for permission to replace it with a multi-storey car park,

54
00:03:22,918 --> 00:03:24,340
but that was refused.

55
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,916
Instead, the company has bought some adjoining land,

56
00:03:26,916 --> 00:03:30,780
and this will be used to increase the number of parking spaces.

57
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:35,510
The Grand, the old cinema in the high street, will close at the end

58
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:36,523
of the year,

59
00:03:36,523 --> 00:03:38,550
and reopen on a different site.

60
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:41,240
You've probably seen the building under construction.

61
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:46,113
The plan is to have three screens with fewer seats, rather than just the

62
00:03:46,113 --> 00:03:48,550
one large auditorium in the old cinema.

63
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:52,700
I expect many of you shop in the indoor market.

64
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:55,586
It's become more and more shabby- looking,

65
00:03:55,586 --> 00:04:00,120
and because of fears about safety, it was threatened with demolition.

66
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:04,986
The good news is that it will close for six weeks to be made safe

67
00:04:04,986 --> 00:04:05,635
and redecorated,

68
00:04:05,635 --> 00:04:08,230
and the improved building will open in July.

69
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:13,708
Lots of people use the library, including school and college students who go there

70
00:04:13,708 --> 00:04:14,490
to study.

71
00:04:14,490 --> 00:04:19,206
The council has managed to secure funding to keep the library open later into

72
00:04:19,206 --> 00:04:20,890
the evening, twice a week.

73
00:04:20,890 --> 00:04:24,813
We would like to enlarge the building in the not-too-distant future,

74
00:04:24,813 --> 00:04:27,310
but this is by no means definite.

75
00:04:27,310 --> 00:04:31,796
There's no limit on access to the nature reserve on the edge of town,

76
00:04:31,796 --> 00:04:34,360
and this will continue to be the case.

77
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:38,544
What will change, though, is that the council will no longer be in charge

78
00:04:38,544 --> 00:04:39,440
of the area.

79
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:45,102
Instead it will become the responsibility of a national body that administers most nature

80
00:04:45,102 --> 00:04:46,720
reserves in the country.

81
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:50,190
OK, now let me ask you...
